Each entry / correction / QC save resolved the base material and design by
loading the WHOLE table and matching in memory — an O(rows) read per save,
twice, that grew every time an import minted a design. Each resolver now tries
the stable unique `code` first (an indexed lookup, the value a name picked from
the list resolves to) and only falls back to the full scan for a genuinely new
or oddly-punctuated name, so the answer is identical and the common save never
scans the table. The two independent lookups in the operator entry and the slab
correction now run together rather than one after the other. No behaviour
change — only far less work on the most-pressed buttons.
