From 9e03e9acb55283ee1392001a2615a6dcb7bc09e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 04:48:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] chromia(qc): deferred Dispatch page, full-record Edit
 incl. QC, Grade+Outcome-only QC
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three related changes to the QC and dispatch flow.

Dispatch is decided at QC but sent later. Grade A → Dispatch no longer captures a
date at QC; the slab is graded and joins a new Dispatch page — a queue of slabs
awaiting dispatch (Dispatch Date shown as "—") on top, a "Dispatched" log below.
Its Action is a date picker plus "Sent for Dispatch", which records the real
dispatch through the existing dispatch logic and will not save without a date.
Stock-then-dispatch stays in the Stockyard's own release log, so the two never
double-count; the dashboard and reports read the same signals as before.

Edit on a slab record now opens the Operator Entry screen with the QC Section
beneath it, pre-filled with every field including the current Grade, Outcome and
Slab Remarks, and saves back onto the SAME record. Correcting the QC reuses the
whole grading path: the current decision (grade decision and its dispatch /
stock / sample / waste record) is undone, then the new grade and outcome are
applied exactly as a first grading would be. History is appended (a CORRECTION
event), never erased. A slab mid-recalibration is out of scope and is sent to
the Recalibration page. The old edit page redirects here.

The QC Section now decides only Grade + Outcome: the Dispatch, Stock and Sample-
cutting date fields are gone (captured on their own screens), while Recalibration
keeps its reason with all its values. The chosen outcome is still written to the
slab's remark behind the scenes, so the Slab Remarks column keeps reading true.
